             Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ) for Qt/CE

Q: Do you support Windows CE 6.0?
A: Yes. Although there will not be a public SDK available by Microsoft
   we do have support for custom SDK created by hardware vendors.

Q: What tools do I need to develop an application with Qt/CE?
A: You need Visual Studio 2005 Standard Edition (or better) and a
   Windows CE 5.0 or Windows Mobile 5.0 SDK (available free from
   Microsoft) or later.

Q: What platforms does Qt/CE support?
A: At the moment we support:
   Windows Mobile 5.0 Pocket PC Edition (ARM)
   Windows Mobile 5.0 Smartphone Edition (ARM)
   Windows CE 5.0 Standard SDK (ARM)
   Windows CE 5.0 Standard SDK (X86)
   Windows CE 5.0 Standard SDK (MIPS)
   Windows CE 5.0 Standard SDK (SH4)
   Windows Mobile 6 Classic (ARM)
   Windows Mobile 6 Standard (ARM)
   Windows Mobile 6 Professional(ARM)

Q: What version of Qt does Qt/CE rely on?
A: On a preview version of the upcoming 4.4.0 release.
